{"name":"Grisaille","hex":"#91979f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grisaille","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["In painting, a method of working which employs only varying values of gray to create form. Often a preliminary step in a fully colored painting.","A stained-glass window in this style."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grisaille"}],"entries":[{"title":"Grisaille","blocks":[{"text":"Grisaille is a painting executed entirely in shades of black and grey or of another neutral greyish colour. It is particularly used in large decorative schemes in imitation of sculpture. Many grisailles include a slightly wider colour range."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Pieter_Bruegel_the_Elder_-_Christ_and_the_Woman_Taken_in_Adultery_-_WGA03469.jpg/330px-Pieter_Bruegel_the_Elder_-_Christ_and_the_Woman_Taken_in_Adultery_-_WGA03469.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grisaille","wikidata":"Q750197"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Del_sarto_Battesimo_della_gente.jpg/500px-Del_sarto_Battesimo_della_gente.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Del_sarto_Battesimo_della_gente.jpg/1280px-Del_sarto_Battesimo_della_gente.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Del_sarto_Battesimo_della_gente.jpg/500px-Del_sarto_Battesimo_della_gente.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Battesimo della gente, one of Andrea del Sarto's gray and brown grisaille frescoes in the Chiostro dello Scalzo, Florence (1511-26)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADel_sarto_Battesimo_della_gente.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons